        <p>SUNDAY SCHOOL SERVICES —The Wesleyan Sunday scheol annivevary sermons were preached in the Wesleyan Church on Sunday, by the Rev T. Oe&amp;n Tayler of Lytham: There were large congregations. The Sunday school children occunied a platform erected near the pulpit, and the singing by them and the choir was very creditable. Dr James Bennett and Mr Henry Ward the einductort, must be coneratulated upon the success attending their efforts in thie respect. The sermon at the morning service was rpacially intended for young people, the subject being " Character Building." Ili the afternoon a spccial flower service was conducted by the Rev T, 0. Taylor. During the singing of a hymn the children attending the schools marched in processional order through the chapel and delivered flowers to the leachers, by whem they were artiatically arranged in a stand near the pulpit. In the evening the chapel was crowded, a large number of friends from Warrington and other parts of the circuit being present. The Rev T. Ogden faylor again occupied the pulpit and preached a moat interesting and instructive sermon. Miss J. Bennett (Lyndhurst). was at the organ. The flowers have been forwarded to the Warrington Infirmary. During the day collections were taken on behalf of the retool funds.</p>
