        <p>"TN THE SPRING TIME A YOUNG MAN'S _L FANCY LIGIITLY TURNS TO THOUGHTS OF LOVE," and having fortunately obtained his fiancee's con- sent to marriage, the important question" Where shall we furnish ?" presents Itself. Both the young people have been very forcibly impressed by the magnificent display in PITTS'S Colossal Showrooms, together with the genuine ring in PITTS'S Advertisements and the uniformly good reputa tion PITTS'S bear, but before tefiaitely deciding they very wisely conchtle to refer the matter to their parents' superior judgm, nt and experience. Upon broaching the subject the unhesitating reply is "CERTAINLY FURNI. H AT PITTo's, like we did nearly thirty years ago. You see the goods are little worse for wear after all these years. PITTS'S occupy the uncommon position of having often furnished three consecutive generations, parents, children, and grand- children, and you cannot po,sibly do better than place the order with that old-established firm." Result, another horse made bright and comfortable at little cost by PITTS'S, to the great satisfaction of all concerned.</p>
