      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-05-18_WidnesExaminer_art0073" n="art0073">
        <head>DOCTOR'S ADVICE.</head>
        <p>DOCTOR'S ADVICE.</p>
        <p>Each season of the year has its peculiar ailments and dangers. We observant person can have failed to notice this. The great prevalence of Influenze during the past season is a striking instance of this fact. Now at this season of the year there are what are known as "Spring Ailments." such as Eczema, Skin Affections, Blood Dis- orders, Pimples, Blotcbee, etc., etc. These ailments, which are so annoying and unpleasant, and indeed, in some cases, dangerous te the human system, can be speedily relieved by a course of Gwilym Evans' Quinine I Bitters, the Vegetable Tunic. This preparation contains the active principle of the. finest Blood Tonics and Purifiers, such as Sarsaparilla, Burdock, Dandelion, Lavender, Saffron, Gentian, and Quinine. The first three of theee plants are noted as Blood Purifiers. 1 Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is admitted to be among the best purifiers of the blood which have yet been dis- covered, and though several vegetable preparations are offered to the public as Blood purifiers, none can coin- I pare with Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters in their efficacy I to attain the desired result. Gwilym Evans' Quinine I Bitters contains no mercury or iron or any other mineral substances, which often leave behind them pernicious effects. This preparation is purely vegetable, and is a natural tonic, being compoeed esitirely of Nature's Remedies, which cannot injure the roost delicate person, while at the 144M8 time it is always effectual and teneficial, when taken, to restore the body to its normal healthy state, la hen any of its organs have been deranged by disease. You are wise if you do the rign thing at the right time. When you need a Tonic try Gwilym Tl"vans' Quinine Bitters, the Acme of Tonics. Try it rive-. A quarter centure's experience, with the testimony cf the public and eminent physicians, prove its wonderful curative character. There is only one first in everything, and first foe the Battle of Strife of Suffering Men and Women stands Owllym Evans' Quinine Bitters the Great Tonic for Poor Blood and Weak Nerves. Do you stiffer from Weakness. Indigestion, and Low Spirits? If so. you may safely pin your faith to Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. The best remedy fot guarding against the dangerous stage of convalescence after influenza is to take liberal doses of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. It averts all fear of relapse, sustains and builds up the system rapidly and permanently. Health hae many hand-muds, and all depend on Strength cf nerve and muscle. We exact too much from these in the daily competitive struggle for success in life, and we have to suffer in consequence. Biliousness, Sleeplessness. Liver Disorders, and chest Affections are all successfully combatted with the sustaining assistarce of Gwilvm Evans Quinine Bitters, which is sold in bottles, 2s. 9d. and 4s. 61. each. Beware of imirations. Note particu- larly the name" Gwilym Evans "on the Label, Stamp, and Bottle (a threefold precaution), without which netts: are genuine. Refuse all (Ahem The Sete Proprietore are The Quinine Bittets Manufacturing Company, Limited' Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
