      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-05-18_WidnesExaminer_art0077" n="art0077">
        <head>cillor Stnethurat and Mr. Geddes.</head>
        <p>cillor Stnethurat and Mr. Geddes.</p>
        <p>Arroncyß DESERTER.—WiIIiam Griffiths was charged with being a deserter from the 3rd Battalion Royal Welsh Fusiliers stationed at Wrexham Barraoks since Jannary Ist He pleaded guilty.—P.s. Cheeney said that in consequenee of information he received he apprebendedtbe prisoner on Tues aay morning and charged him with being a deserter from the above regiment. He admitted that he hail deserted Prisoner was remanded to await an escort and the officer was recommended for the usual rewar.i.</p>
