        <p>HAYDOCIC PARR RACW.B.—Temporary authority was granted to Richard Jownecn and Samuel Hurst to sell intoxic iting liquo, aat Haydocx Park tiacecourse on the 18th and 19th May. DRUNKENNESS - Peter Jones was fined 25 63 and costs for being drunk and Oiso,derlv at, liar:olwo,d on the 6th May; John Mullin was mulcted in a like penalty for a similar elfence at Harlestown on the 19th or April ; and I.l:chael Aldet,o who did not appear, was fined 5s and costs for being drunk and disorderly at Buctonwood. A NEGLIGENT CYCLIS r.—For riding a bicycle at Poulton- with-Foarnhead on the 'Bth ult. without a lighted lamp at 10,20 p m.. Peter Curdiffe wea fined Is. and costs.</p>
        <p>_ AN UNLICENSED DOG —Andrew Starkey. of Burton wood. was summoned for keeping a dog without a licenca on the 3rd inst. On a constable visiting the premises Le found a cross bred Trl,h terriar there, and when asked to oroduei license excuaed himself by saying that he was keeping the dog for ancther ma'.'. fie was fined Is. ed. and costs AN AILL)URIVED .:C/IDOL ATTENDANCE t).SE.—li;cigar _Hatton was summoned for neglecting to cause his child to attend school regularly. - The Clerk stated that the case was ad- journed in order that certificates respecting the chilli's health might be produced.—Mr. Shearer said the certificates produced were undated but he thought the child had been unwell and under the °ire ,mstances he would withdraw the case.—This course was agreed to.</p>
