        <p>BRITISH WORKMAN'S AND GENERAL ASSURANCE COMPANY 9 LIMITED • CHIEF OFFICES :—B ROAD STREET CORNER; BIRITUGHAIIis EXTRACTS FROM DIRECTORS' REPORT FOR EIGHT MONTHS ENDING DECEMBER 31sT, 1899. During the eight menthe ending 31st December last, the sum of £60,161 has been ADDED TO THE ASSURANCE FUND—the largest increase ever made during a similar period. The INCREASE in the PREMIUM INCOME during the same period was £3S,BB9—EQUIVALENT to an increase ef over £53,000 per annum. NEW BUsI NESS F)R THE EIGHT MONTHS. ORDINARY DEPARTMENT.—The numbet of New proposals received was 3,357, assuring the SUM of £224,034, at a Yearly Premium of £12,698. The number of Policies issued was 3,023, assuring the sum of £199.138 at an Annual Premium of £11,358. INDUSTRIAL DEPARTMENT.—The number of Policies issued wa5.249,943 at an Annual Premium of £157,710. EIGHT MONTHS' CLAIMS. ORDINARY DEPARTMENT.—The amount paid in Claims during the E'ght Months in this Department was £23,137, including £911„ Surrender Claims. INDUSTRIAL DEPARTMENT.—The amount paid in Claims during the Eight Months in this Department •, was £169,679, including £11,435 Surrender Claims. The TOTAL AMOUNT paid to the 31st December, 1899, was £2,540,637. RESULTS OF THE EIGHT MONTHS' TRA `NT S A.O - The Total Income of the Company was £443,613, and the Total Payments £375,157, leaving a S,,rplus Balance on the Eight Months' Accounts of £68,445. Out of this sum £3,235 has been written off investments, Loans, Furniture, Ste., leaving £60,161 to be added to the Assurance Fund. The Funds now stand at FIVE HUNDRED AND NINA THOUSAND POUNDS. As the result of LESS THAN THREE YEARS' painstaking and economical management. the INCOME of the Company has been INCREASED BY OVER £145,000 per annum, whilst the Assurance Fund has been PRACTICALLY DOUBLED. LOCAL DISTRICT OFFICE : UNION BANK CHAMBERS, MARKET GATE, WARRINGTON. T. BOYD, SUPERIXTENDENT, 78, WIDNES ROAD, WIDNES. W. J. YATES, SUPERINTENDENT.</p>
